  "limitations": [
    "All source hashes and climate values are synthetic. Prospective request-derived revision keys are distributed sequentially over actual sorted coverage pair routes; this is not the geographic attribution of acquisition rectangles to real cell observations.",
    "The supervisor sampled logical file lengths in the whole output directory, not NTFS allocated cluster bytes. Its filesystem free-space reserve is separate. This clarification supersedes physical-disk wording in the raw worker receipt.",
    "The peak RSS is a sampled observation of the main Node process, not a sum across the process tree. The Windows Job independently enforced the declared process-tree committed-memory cap, process count and wall-time deadline. Disk sampling ran at 60-second start intervals; publication writes also used immediate shared byte budgets.",
    "The complete publisher/global-tree proof and selected runtime routes passed. Full operator closure was exercised in focused fixtures but was not separately measured at this 18-million-row scale.",
    "This proof establishes bounded synthetic lineage engineering acceptance only. It does not establish real ERA5 data completeness, request feasibility, acquisition authorization, deployment, installed serving coverage or free-host feasibility.",
    "No source downloads, external requests, credential access, deployment or runtime selection were performed. All scratch and failed-conflict output was retained. There was one supervised full proof and no automatic retry.",
    "Raw receipts and bulky synthetic artifacts remain local ignored data. Published source normalization records four unchanged legacy files whose measured checkout bytes used CRLF while Git stores LF; measured pins and the executable bundle are preserved unchanged."
